{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Reuben found mandrakes in the field.</b> The mandrakes (דודאים) have the form of a human being — they possess the likeness of a head and hands — and they are efficacious for pregnancy. This is by way of a special property (סגולה) inherent in them, not by way of nature, for their manner of generation is astonishing. But the fruit, which is like the form of apples, has a good fragrance; hence Scripture says (Song of Songs 7:14): ״הדודאים נתנו ריח״. And Reuben did not bring his mother the root but only the fruit, for her to delight in it and enjoy its fragrance; and through this she sought to honor Jacob by perfuming his bed, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 7:17): ״נפתי משכבי מור אהלים וקנמון״. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:29.776893736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}